    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d801">

                <pb facs="0730" n="646" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp02/pg646"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72114/3250</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Great
                        Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Page</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-02-18T17:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 18, 1918, 5 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>6609. Your 8455, January 31, 2 p.m. While the Department has not made public any
                    statement regarding its negative attitude towards <pb facs="0731" n="647"
                        xml:id="pg647"/> relief of Russian prisoners in Germany in the present
                    circumstances, it has requested the appropriate authorities not to grant
                    licenses for the transmission of food, and has asked the Red Cross here, to
                    which license had been granted for the transmission of funds for Allied
                    prisoners in enemy countries, to discourage for the present any applications in
                    favor of Russian prisoners.</p>
                <p>It is recommended that correspondence mentioned be detained.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
